WEBVTT

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.860
The number of views has been declining.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:27.940
FIRE VS ICE

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.820
The latest video, Gas flame vs Ice magic,
seems unpopular.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.400
The comments were harsh, like,
"A pointless waste of resources."

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.160
We must tighten up our budget from today.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.240
I will stop bidding on online auctions.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.870
-What's that?
-I got it at last.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.960
This magazine listed the final result
of SEGA SATURN readers' choice.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.550
Unfortunately, I hadn't had the chance
to see the results.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.630
COLLECTOR'S EDITION

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.220
I couldn't die without knowing it.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:01.640
Maybe this desire kept me alive
in the harsh other world.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.770
Such a silly thing kept you alive?

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:04.980
-Takafumi.
-What?

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.440
The results are here.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.440
The last page of SEGA SATURN's history is…

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.690
SATURN GAMES
ARE THE WORLD'S #1

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.110
…in this magazine.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.200
Stunningly, I don't care.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.160
The very last game
that came in the first place was…

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.030
Are you reading it already?

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:27.920
Oh, the winner was a bishojo game
ported from the PC version.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.590
I guess the results weren't
what you hoped for.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.000
No, I'm not complaining.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.420
I can agree with the ranking
as I read the reviews.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.850
But I feel sad, as if I were watching
wild, macho high-school boys

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.680
getting tamed by girlfriends.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.770
Really?

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.810
-Not really.
-What?

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:16.380
Guardian Heroes should have been
number one!

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:20.970
It adopted the fighting game system into
a side-scroller while maintaining balance.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.810
Its innovation and perfection
has got to be recognized!

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.770
197th place? What?

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:32.360
197th place?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.240
UNCLE:
YOU'RE FINE THE WAY YOU ARE

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.150
GET HOME

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.400
SOLD CHEAPER THAN A SCOURING PAD

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.870
One of the original SATURN RPGs
was placed in second.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.130
I didn't play RPG at all.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.210
What?

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.590
The beginning went okay.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.010
YOU NEED SALT TO KILL SLUGS

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.430
But I couldn't remember what I did
the day before…

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.720
WHY DO I NEED SALT?

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.050
…and got lost.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.810
Did you?

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:33.600
I mean, I had an encounter
like an RPG game in the other world.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:34.850
What?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.440
Icuras elran.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:41.070
You fucking orc.
I won't lose to a fugly pig like you.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.650
What is this?

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.570
This was the time right after I arrived
at the village.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.200
Let's fast-forward it.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.700
Uncle, whenever you got to a village,
you found yourself in a battle.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.250
Well, in the flame shrine
at the west end of the village,

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.250
the legendary blaze dragon has roused.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.550
The village will be burned down
if we don't do anything.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:08.260
The only way to slay the blaze dragon is
using the Ice clan's god freezing sword.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:13.220
However, the descendant of the Ice clan
is a bit of a pain in the neck.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.950
Her name is Mabel.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.830
Unless we melt the ice,
trapping her heart,

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.410
we can't break the seal
of the god freezing sword.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.040
When I was little,

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.050
I saw powa-powa blossoms with my mom
at the top of Mount Marchid.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:48.010
That was beautiful.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.110
I went straight to the shrine of flame
and slew the legendary blaze dragon.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:07.990
How come?

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:13.030
Seriously, it was hard. But I killed it
after I got its offensive strategy down.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:17.410
Not like that! You should've gone
to Mount Marchid for powa-powa blossoms.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.080
I couldn't remember that.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.000
It's not that complicated.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.590
What?
You defeated the legendary blaze dragon?

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.310
Thank you very much.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:36.020
They were so grateful.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:38.850
Yeah.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:44.400
I got it.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:53.160
SEGA SATURN Console and 20 games.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.790
Takafumi, was that a package delivery?

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:00.250
Oh, well… this is…

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:07.210
It was a surprise gift for him,
but he just said we've got to save up.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.720
This…

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:18.810
What?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.310
Huh?

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.280
Is he happy or furious?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.780
It's a bit early,
but happy birthday, Uncle.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.910
Oh, by the way…

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.830
I found Guardian Heroes.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.720
Want to play?

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.260
I worried in vain.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:58.310
For my uncle, spending money
on a SEGA console can't be a waste.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:16.240
The town trampled down in Alien Storm
looked like this.

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:19.040
When it is deserted and chilly,

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.120
I can feel the tension in the air.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:25.170
Yeah. It's totally different
from New Year's Eve in the other world.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.460
What? Uncle!

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.260
-Do you want to know?
-Yes.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:41.270
"If aliens were to invade the earth now,

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:45.650
would you be an ordinary citizen
who runs for your life, or"…

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:47.190
That was the tagline of the game.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:50.650
-Players, as one of the Alien Busters--
-No, not the game!

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.110
Is that a comic magazine?

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:59.660
Yeah. I haven't spent New Year's Eve
reading a manga in a long time.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:01.950
Can you follow the story
after a 17-year break?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.410
KochiKame would follow the same plot
all the time.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.040
KochiKame's serialization is over.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.630
Really? I never thought it would end.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.340
You won't find it.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:18.890
I'm more interested in the story
of the other world than the manga.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.600
Not on the contents page either.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:23.850
Seriously?

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.600
Icuras elran.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:31.360
It's not a big deal, but it's something
like a New Year's Eve party.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:33.190
It's a thanksgiving festival

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:35.440
for the gods' protection
against the hardships of winter.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.410
The lord would feed you a splendid dinner.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:38.490
Cheers!

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.490
That's some feast.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:45.580
The residents of the other world
were pumped up for this festival.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.290
For the festival, I also…

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:51.960
All right, we gonna have a great time!

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.380
Yeah!

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.220
Well, I wish I could be like that.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:09.020
I couldn't be a totally different person
from who I was.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.770
I ate alone and went back to my room.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:17.700
What?

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.320
It was great.
I enjoyed the roasted chicken--

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:24.620
I'm not talking about the food.
Was that all for the festival?

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.500
-Yeah.
-Where was she? The tsun--

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.830
The bad-mouthing girl?

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.420
She was not there,
and nothing happened after that.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.850
Do you wanna play on the SATURN?

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:46.520
Let's do that!

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.440
Pew pew!

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:52.440
You'll break the buttons.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:56.650
By the way, Mabel came to my room
after the festival.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.490
The protector of the god freezing sword.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:00.030
Now, the battle begins!

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.620
I want to hear about that!

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.040
-I thought we finally finished talking--
-Hurry up!

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.830
Well… nothing really happened.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.080
See?

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.930
MEMORY -
SHOW A PIECE OF YOURSELF

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.800
Why are you here?

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.560
I wanted you to tell me.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:33.270
You slew the dragon single-handedly.
I want to be strong like you.

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:37.820
How can I stop being a coward?

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.780
"Stop being a coward"?

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.160
Who said that you are a coward?

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.910
-What?
-Who said that?

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:49.660
The village mayor.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:53.120
Live your life the way you want to,

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:57.590
not by someone else's ways.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:06.390
I believe strength is the power
to carry this through.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:14.980
Great. That's so cool, Uncle.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.230
Mabel being like this!

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:24.320
Like this, Uncle must have gradually built
relationships in the other world.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.410
How have you spent your life until now?

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:35.370
I have been a recluse
and closed off my heart.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:38.840
That's fine.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.210
What? But…

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.340
That's completely fine.

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:46.930
No matter what people said,
I never gave up being a SEGA user

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.680
and never will.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:54.640
Is your role to be an ordinary citizen
who buys a popular console?

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:56.940
Or…

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.280
Are you sure?

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.530
Yes, I'm sure.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.120
Incredible!

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:19.210
-She chose her life and went back home.
-I'm so happy to stay reclusive.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.340
Oh, she gave me the sword.

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:25.050
-Please keep the god freezing sword.
-Thanks, but no thanks. It's cold.

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:26.970
Really?

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:28.680
No, I declined the offer.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:31.060
Well… that's about it.

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:36.770
Uncle, would you care for
a bowl of soba noodles?

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:39.480
That's a good idea. Let's boil the water.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:48.820
What did you do on New Year's Eve
when you were a student? Play games?

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:52.830
Well, I watched TV. Something like
an It's Okay to Laugh! special episode.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:55.870
It was a special occasion
as students couldn't watch daytime shows.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.580
That show ended too.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.880
Seriously? How is that possible?

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:00.960
Finito.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:04.550
Well, it's been 17 years. No wonder.

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:06.470
But the show was on until three years ago.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.680
It lasted that long? That's awesome!

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:11.430
-KochiKame ended last year.
-What?

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.810
What kind of shows do you like, Takafumi?

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:16.310
I don't think you've watched it,
but Not Okay to Laugh.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.520
No way! What happened with Tamori?

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.690
It's not the sequel.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.320
It seems like he'd watched TV a lot.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:27.740
Playing games, chatting,
and slurping soba…

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:29.490
and that's how the new year rolled in.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:35.240
JANUARY, 2018

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:49.380
The breeze you just made was quite sharp.

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:53.640
Let's keep it that way all day today.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:58.850
No way, you are kidding again.

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:02.190
I should avoid this street from now on.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:03.360
Fujimiya?

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.450
Takafumi?

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:12.070
I thought so!

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.620
You can't be this tall!

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:17.330
I hit a growth spurt in high school.
It's been such a long time.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:19.410
Yeah.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.300
How are you doing these days?

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.550
A lot happened, and I'm working part-time.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:35.970
I see. I'm going to college.

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.100
It's chilly.

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:41.310
Do you wanna stop by my place?
It's close by.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:43.850
Your parents' house?

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:44.940
No.

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:50.900
I'll come by
after dropping off the groceries.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.490
Okay, here is the address.

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:56.530
30 MINUTES LATER

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.080
Takafumi?

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.000
TAKAFUMI:
I'M GRABBING SOME SNACKS.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.460
GO INSIDE WITHOUT ME.
THE DOOR'S UNLOCKED.

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:12.550
Hi, I'm coming in.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:52.720
Stonagas resto rarbarum.

00:16:57.590 --> 00:16:59.050
Icuras cuora.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:04.600
Icuras cuora. Icuras cuora.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.980
Gotta use Japanese.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:11.230
-Spirits of memory, deliver unto oblivion.
-Uncle!

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:18.870
Takafumi, the enemy… She saw it.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.700
Erase-- Erasing her memory faster,

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:25.210
-means less impact on her mind.
-She's my friend!

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:30.920
A… friend?

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:34.630
Thank you for being friends with Takafumi.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:40.720
-Well, that was…
-I cast in Granbahamal lingo.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:41.810
Like a dialect?

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:46.390
So, Takafumi is supporting an uncle
who hasn't worked for 17 years.

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:49.770
I am a YouTuber.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:53.780
I saw him mumbling to himself out there.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:57.110
Occasionally, I chat with spirits
to sharpen my magic skills.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.360
He's seriously crazy!

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.410
Yes, it's crazy.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.410
Because he returned from another world
and does magic.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:08.330
I practice magic
and my YouTube channel showcases it.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:12.000
Then do the goddamn magic now!

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:16.090
Well… I can't do it for free.
I'm a YouTuber with two million views.

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.380
-Right?
-Yeah.

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:19.840
What is the basis of his professionalism?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:25.180
Anyway, you shouldn't hinder
Takafumi's life anymore.

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:28.390
Oh, I see.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:31.810
You like Takafumi.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.110
No, no, no, no, no. It's not that.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:38.490
100% no. We are just friends.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:42.950
It shouldn't be the case.
I understand mature love.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.910
I watched the entire Evangelion series
when I was in junior high.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.580
You watched Eva?

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:52.170
Yes, I did. Everyone did.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:19:00.130
At that time, SEGA was one of the sponsors
of Evangelion.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.090
In the end, it's because of SEGA.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.180
Well, then you know Asuka too?

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.930
The girl in the red suit, right?

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:12.020
Oh, shit! Uncle may catch on
to the tsundere concept!

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:15.150
Don't you misunderstand.
You are indebted to me now.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:16.980
That's not what I meant.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.610
I didn't mean "together forever"
or anything.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.990
He may realize what
that elfin girl really meant.

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:25.080
Did you know?

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:29.290
Actually, Asuka has a crush on Kaji.

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:35.670
Sorry, Takafumi,
you may be too inexperienced

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:38.210
to notice her crush on Kaji.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.090
What? Yeah.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.510
SO SHALLOW…!!!

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:46.010
Stop fooling around already.

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:49.640
Don't make assumptions
based on an anime's views on love.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:52.690
You're right. Let's talk about real love.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:56.650
Her name was Kaede Nanase.

00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:01.740
The enemy stole her mind,
and she lost her old self.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:07.780
Her affection soon turned
into lethal intention in battle.

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:11.210
However, after a long battle,
she got a sure response.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:12.750
Joy.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:16.540
She regained herself
under the bursting flash.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:20.550
"Who did I kill?"

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.430
"What did I lose?"

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:29.680
There is no such a thing as "too early"
to express your affection.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:31.980
Oh, my God.

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:35.940
The resolution gap between anime
and games is too big.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:37.610
Hey, Fujimiya.

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:38.860
What?

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:41.360
That was just a story from a video game.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.440
Wow--

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.990
-Just a fiction?
-A fiction?

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.450
No, I experienced it firsthand.

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:49.660
You, shut your…

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.960
Spirits of memory, investigate now.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:04.380
"Geez, he has a roommate. I feel stupid
for being psyched and changing my outfit."

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:06.680
-What?
-True, you're wearing a different outfit.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:07.840
No, it's the same one.

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:09.430
You even took a shower.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:10.930
No, I didn't.

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.270
Who is there?

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:19.110
A mind reader, or con man?

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:23.490
What are you?

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:29.530
I am just an uncle…

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.790
back from another world--

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:34.250
Mr. Shibazaki, I got a package for you.

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:36.870
-Mr. Shibazaki?
-I'm coming.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:37.960
Mr. Shibazaki?

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:40.090
You've got to cut ties, Takafumi.

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.710
Seriously, you need to get out.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:45.630
If you can't afford the rent,
I will cover it by taking on a job.

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:47.930
-Seriously? Want to be my roommate?
-What?

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:51.350
-I see, that's definitely an option.
-Well, I didn't mean that--

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:53.970
But I've got my uncle with me.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:59.310
What's in there?
This box weighs 15 kilograms.

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:01.770
-It's a bag of rice.
-Rice?

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:04.780
Can you accept my scribbled signature?

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:09.990
One additional person now knows
my uncle in real life.

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:13.950
He looked somewhat more cheerful
than his usual self.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:18.370
And I'll refrain from buying rice online…

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.500
I felt a lethal intent.

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:50.920
Subtitle translation by:
Naoka Matsumura
